  "limitations": [
    "This is sequential frame sample-time replay, not live USB/queue/CPU wall-time validation; the unchanged 8 s hardware point deadline still applies.",
    "Round 2 had already been inspected during diagnosis and is a temporal check, not a blind holdout. Historical and synthetic regressions influenced selection.",
    "Final B repeats two of four originally valid neighbors within their saved traces. Points 8 and 31 stop before B finishes; those short files cannot establish live failure or success. The same originally accepted windows still pass unchanged quality gates.",
    "Zero acceptances in 80 synthetic noise sequences per policy is bounded test evidence, not a universal false-acceptance-rate guarantee. Policies reuse the same seeds.",
    "Point 9 remains invalid; raw records and historical valid flags are never rewritten.",
    "No warm start is adopted. Only failed windows can become a longer candidate prefix; accepted VERIFY and MEASURE remain independent.",
    "The newly accepted historical 38 kHz trace has a persistent exact-frequency spectral component, but no external RF ground truth. The original conditional half-window rule remains: halves are required only when the wide-band peak lies outside target tolerance.",
    "The preserved late-target example is accepted at 7.12 s rather than the v5 4.92 s; the new schedule is not uniformly faster across all arrival times."
  ],
